-- =============================================================================
-- Data of the e2e tests (dashboard/tests/testthat), loaded by setup.R into a blank Postgres
--
-- Only rows: the 5 gold tables (210 lots, from the local database used before Neon)
-- and the user "test" at the end. The tables and views are created before, from
-- include/sql/create_gold.sql, so the tests always check the current views.
--
-- When it has to change:
-- - A view changes: nothing to do. The views come from create_gold.sql on every run.
-- - The columns of a gold table change: a removed or renamed column, or a new NOT NULL one
--   without a default, makes the load fail. A new column that allows NULL loads empty.
--
-- How to regenerate it: always from the old local database, never from Neon. The tests rely on
-- these lots (e.g. the only marker in Valladolid, the lots active on 2026-11-18), and Neon's change.
--   1. Start the old database on its volume, under another name than the tests' container:
--        docker run -d --rm --name subastas-db-old --env-file subastas-db.env \
--          -v subastas-analytics_42239a_subastas_db_data:/var/lib/postgresql/data postgres:17
--   2. A change in silver (the most likely, e.g. a new field extracted by Claude or Goolzoom):
--      this database's silver doesn't have it, and filling it for real would mean paying Claude
--      or Goolzoom again. Add the column to its silver table with ALTER TABLE, fill it with
--      made-up values that make sense for the tests, and go on with step 3.
--   3. Rebuild its gold with the current code: drop the gold tables, then run the current
--      include/sql/create_gold.sql and include/sql/load_gold.sql. Gold is built only from silver.
--   4. Dump it again (data only, as COPY blocks that name their columns), from the repo's root:
--        docker exec -e PGPASSWORD=subastas_app subastas-db-old \
--          pg_dump -U subastas_app -h localhost -d subastas \
--            --data-only --no-owner --no-privileges \
--            -t gold.dim_date -t gold.dim_auctions -t gold.dim_catastral_references \
--            -t gold.fact_lots -t gold.lots_catastral_references_bridge \
--          > dashboard/tests/e2e_data.sql
--   5. Add this header and the user "test" at the end again: the dump replaces the whole file.
--
-- \restrict and \unrestrict are added by recent pg_dump versions: load the file with the
-- psql of the postgres:17 container
-- =============================================================================

--
-- PostgreSQL database dump
--

